.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt AUDIT_TOKEN_GET 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm audit_token_get ,
.Nm audit_token_check
.Nd get and check the audit token of a process
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In bsm/audit.h
.Ft int
.Fn audit_token_get "int pd" "pid_t pid" "int flags" "audit_token_t *token"
.Ft int
.Fn audit_token_check "const audit_token_t *token" "int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An audit token
.Pq Vt audit_token_t , see Xr audit_token 3
names one process at one point of its life: its process ID, a lifetime ID
that is never reused, the exec generation, the image ID, and the jail, user,
group and audit IDs it had when the token was taken.
It is opaque; the
.Fn audit_token_to_*
functions of
.Xr audit_token 3
read it.
.Pp
The
.Fn audit_token_get
system call stores in
.Fa token
the token of a process:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa pd No \&>= 0"
.It Fa pd No \&>= 0
the process the process descriptor
.Fa pd
refers to
.Pq see Xr pdfork 2 ;
.Fa pid
must be 0.
The descriptor needs the
.Dv CAP_PDGETPID
right and is all the authority the call needs.
.It Fa pd No = \-1 , Fa pid No = 0
the calling process.
.It Fa pd No = \-1 , Fa pid No > 0
the process with process ID
.Fa pid ,
if the caller may see it
.Pq the rule of Xr ps 1 .
.El
.Pp
A process that has begun to exit, or has exited and not been waited for,
is refused unless
.Fa flags
has
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXIT .
.Pp
The
.Fn audit_token_check
system call tells whether the process
.Fa token
names still exists: a process with the token's process ID, lifetime ID and
exec generation.
In
.Fa flags ,
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXEC
accepts any exec generation of the process, and
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXIT
accepts a process that has exited and has not been waited for.
A process the caller may not see is reported as not existing.
.Pp
The IDs are counters, not secrets: knowing a token gives no access to the
process it names.
.Pp
Use
.Xr pdopentoken 2
to get a process descriptor for the process a token names.
.Ss Capability mode
In capability mode
.Pq see Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Fn audit_token_get
accepts a process descriptor and the calling process, but not a process ID,
and
.Fn audit_token_check
matches only the calling process and its descendants, so that a sandbox
cannot probe the process table.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn audit_token_get
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa flags
has a bit other than
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXIT ,
.Fa pid
is negative, or
.Fa pd
is a descriptor and
.Fa pid
is not 0.
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa pd
is less than \-1, is not an open descriptor, or is not a process
descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
.Fa pd
lacks the
.Dv CAP_PDGETPID
right.
.It Bq Er ECAPMODE
A process ID was given in capability mode.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
The process does not exist, the caller may not see it, or it has exited
and
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXIT
was not given.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa token
points outside the process's address space.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fn audit_token_check
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa flags
has a bit other than
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXEC
and
.Dv AUDIT_TOKEN_MAY_EXIT .
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa token
points outside the process's address space.
.It Bq Er ESRCH
No process matches the token, or the caller may not see it.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr pdopentoken 2 ,
.Xr audit_token 3 ,
.Xr audit 4 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn audit_token_get
and
.Fn audit_token_check
system calls first appeared in 5BSD; the token follows the audit token of
macOS.
